-- Transcription of layout-language-consult.md §5.4 (lines 545-583),
-- clean-room LengYue, landscape class. Disclosed adjustments:
--   - no-op root sizing supplied (document elides it, same as all five
--     encodings — see q5go.lyt's comment for the full reasoning).
--   - `T(...)[BLACK BOX]{pref 1fr, min envelope over tabs}`: the bare
--     "min envelope over tabs" prose isn't a literal value, so 'min' is
--     omitted here and the compiler derives the T-node's structural
--     minimum as the componentwise max of its children (§4.1 line
--     298-302).
--   - the five bare `CP-library, CP-cards, CP-settings, CP-analysis,
--     CP-other` names inside T(...) (line 576) aren't bracketed
--     `widgetid[domain,...]` leaves at all — they're prose naming the
--     control-panel tabs, which §2 explicitly commissions as an opaque
--     black box outside the A/go|common|debug|board classification. We
--     give each one domain='blackbox' (the sixth domain literal added in
--     lyt_ast.py specifically for this region) and no facets.
--   - `A_go[go, action]{28px}`, `A_common[common, action]{28px}`: the
--     bare-fixed-extent shorthand (min=pref=max=28px).
--   - `I_engine[...]{28px, envelope: {...}}`: fixed 28px reservation with
--     an attached (documentation-only, for this 1-D sizing model) content
--     state list; states renamed to valid identifiers
--     (`connected_5digit_latency` for the document's
--     "connected×latency≤5digits", since '×' and '≤' aren't legal
--     identifier characters).
--   - F4 DISCLOSURE (review row 1609,
--     .claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-compiler-prototype-review.md finding
--     F4 item 4): every one of the T(...)'s six children below is given
--     its own `min WRAPPER_MIN` (300px). §5.4's own text (line 577) gives
--     no such per-child min — the bare "min envelope over tabs" phrase is
--     prose, not a value, and the compiler derives the T-node's OWN
--     structural min as the componentwise max of its children's declared
--     mins (§4.1 line 298-302). Left with no per-child min at all, that
--     derivation would yield T's own min = 0px, which reads as "the
--     black-box region gets no floor at all" — an equally unfaithful
--     reading of the same prose. We import WRAPPER_MIN onto every child
--     instead, so the derived T floor is a real, if approximate, 300px —
--     the SAME choice lengyue_portrait.lyt already makes (with 200px,
--     disclosed there). An earlier version of this file made the same
--     choice WITHOUT disclosing it; this paragraph brings the two files'
--     disclosure to parity rather than removing the (functionally
--     necessary) per-child mins.
--   - AMENDMENT 3 (ledger row 1715, gap-amendment-build): two `gap`
--     declarations, both mapped onto `frontend/src/assets/css/theme.css`'s
--     `--space-*` tier scale (that file's own §"Four tiers for gap,
--     padding, margin", read in full):
--       - the OUTER H(...) (board area vs. the side control column) gets
--         `gap 12px`, `--space-medium` ("section-level gap, content-block
--         separation") — for the split between the page's two MAJOR
--         REGIONS. DISCLOSED DOWN-TIER FROM `--space-loose` (20px): the
--         first probe used `--space-loose`, which re-solves OPTIMAL at
--         every representative/OVERLAY_SIZES size EXCEPT `900x600`
--         (landscape), a size that solved OPTIMAL pre-amendment (gap 0)
--         and regresses to INFEASIBLE at `--space-loose` specifically
--         because of the extra reserved gap width — a real, measured
--         finding, not silently dropped. `--space-medium` (12px) restores
--         `900x600` to OPTIMAL while every OTHER size's feasibility
--         status is unchanged from BOTH the gap-0 baseline and the
--         `--space-loose` probe (see build report's feasibility table for
--         the full before/after grid, including the two INFEASIBLE sizes
--         — `1280x1024` and the `1080x1920`-viewport-fed-to-the-landscape-
--         class probe — that were ALREADY infeasible before this
--         amendment, per fix1's own X6 disclosure, and remain so
--         independent of gap tier).
--       - the side column's own V(...) (the go-actions/engine-info/
--         common-actions strip stack feeding the black-box T node) gets
--         `gap 4px`, `--space-tight` ("button-cluster gaps, icon
--         spacing, tight rows") — the narrowest tier, matching that
--         comment's own words almost verbatim: this IS a stack of tight
--         control rows. Already the smallest tier, so no down-tier
--         probe was possible for this one; it did not need one --
--         re-solving with only this gap (root gap held at 0) never
--         introduced a new infeasibility at any tested size.
layout lengyue-landscape =
  {min 0px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 12px} H(
    {pref 1fr} V(
      {pref maximize, aspect 1} B[board],
      {min 24px, pref 24px, max 24px} I_board[board, info],
      {min 28px, pref 28px, max 28px} A_board[board, action]
    ),
    {min 340px, pref 32fr, max 340px+60ch, gap 4px} V(
      {28px} A_go[go, action],
      {28px, envelope: {disconnected, connected_5digit_latency}} I_engine[common, info],
      {28px} A_common[common, action],
      {pref 1fr} T(
        {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} tree[board, info+action],
        {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-library[blackbox],
        {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-cards[blackbox],
        {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-settings[blackbox],
        {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-analysis[blackbox],
        {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-other[blackbox]
      )[BLACK BOX]
    )
  )
